      "id": "source-74-one-tray-contact-rod-and-all-line-waves",
      "description": "Fresh canonical pixels: one oblique rectangular tray with rim, front wall, right wall, water surface and two small dark underside support tabs. One thin diagonal rod lightly touches the water; its horizontal handle enters from the left and joins it near the upper half. Sixteen wavefront lines: three left of the contact rod, thirteen right of it. The first right-hand wave has a bent upper tip (about x250,y50); it is a wave, not another rod. Approximate back/front scan intercept pairs are retained in the external inventory. The rod and handle occlude parts of the first three waves. All wave endpoints/midpoints, contact locations and tray/rod/handle vertices map to within-group relations; wavefronts stay inside the common water surface. Exact straightness and parallelism regularize the scan, with the same side ordering. No arrows, numbers, labels, new scales or deep immersion.",
